#! btw 1
#! name: pattern-sugar
#! license: CC0-1.0
#! visibility: public
# pattern-sugar: short ways to write patterns. x:4 is x x x x and x~4 is x ~ ~ ~; ply doubles each step in its slot;
# poly walks a 3- or 5-step pattern 8 steps a bar, so it drifts against the kick; off stacks a copy one step later an
# octave up; iter starts the riff a quarter later each bar; palindrome plays it there and back. Each is written out
# before it plays, so this is the same song as its longhand: btw same-as says so.
tempo 126
key am

section groove 8 bars {
  deck A: kick x~4 x~4 x~4 x~4 | hihat ply([~ x ~ x?], 2) vel=50..80 | clap poly(8, [~ ~ x]) vel=70
  deck B: bass a1~2 a1 ~ c2~3 e2 g1~4 ~~4 | melody off([a4 ~ c5 ~ e5 ~ ~ ~], 1, 12) inst=pluck
}
section turn 8 bars {
  deck A: kick x:4 | hihat poly(8, [x x ~ x ~]) vel=45..75 | snare ~ x ~ x
  deck B: bass palindrome([a1 c2 e2 g2]) | melody iter([a4 c5 e5 g5 e5 c5 ~ ~], 4) inst=pluck
}
arrange groove turn groove
